.TH tupngdraw 1 0.7 tclutils "Tcl Utility Command"
.SH NAME
tupngdraw \- thin CLI wrapper for tclutils::tupngdraw
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tupngdraw demo <out.png> ?-width N? ?-height N?
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The tupngdraw command is a thin wrapper around the Tcl package
tclutils::tupngdraw, a pure-Tcl 2D drawing layer that renders to a PNG via
tclutils::tupng (no Tk, no external packages).
.PP
The wrapper renders a self-contained demo image (overlapping translucent
discs, a filled triangle, strokes) to the given file and prints its path.
The primary interface is the Tcl library; see tupngdraw(n) for the drawing
object, its methods, options, and semantics.
.PP
.nf
tclsh bin/tupngdraw.tcl demo out.png -width 320 -height 200
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tupng(n), tuimage(n)
